2026-11-27 19:52:05.007 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have to stop here: every write tool is being refused.\n\n**Status: no changes were made.** All three write paths failed with the same class of error:\n\n- `terminal` → `Sandboxed execution refused: SANDBOX_POLICY=auto and no OS sandbox backend is available on this host, while caller_scope=subagent has no operator approval path.`\n- `execute_code` / `python_repl` → same refusal (`PTC has no operator approval path`)\n- `patch_file` and `write_file` → `Tool is not allowed during a background review. Execution has been skipped.`\n\nSo I could not edit files, could not create `meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs`, and could not run `cargo check` / `cargo test`. The repo is untouched (no commits, no edits).\n\n**What I did complete — full design, ready to apply verbatim:**\n\n1. `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs`\n   - `mod coalescer;` added to the module list (alphabetically before `concatenator`).\n   - `optimize()` final collect gains `.map(coalescer::coalesce)` after `.map(|rule| restorer::restore_on_err(rule, &optimized_map))`.\n   - Two new `OptimizedExpr` variants: `CharClass(Vec<(String, String)>)` and `NegCharClass(Vec<(String, String)>)`, with `Display` arms `[a..z, A..Z]` / `![a..z, A..Z]` (char literals via `{:?}`). They are leaves: `map_top_down`, `map_bottom_up`, `iter_top_down` all hit their existing `expr => expr` / `_ =>` arms, so no changes needed there.\n\n2. `meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs` (new, ~250 lines, fully drafted) — `pub fn coalesce(rule) -> rule` using `expr.map_top_down(coalesce_expr)`:\n   - `flatten_choice` walks the right-nested `Choice` chain left-to-right; `build_choice` rebuilds it right-nested.\n   - `alternative_ranges`: `Str` with exactly 1 char → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens` 1 char → both cases if `is_alphabetic()` else `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → absorbed; `RestoreOnErr(inner)` → recurse (wrapper stripped); anything else → `None` (does not qualify).\n   - `merge_ranges`: sort by start code point, merge when `next.start <= current.end + 1` (overlap **and** adjacency), ascending output.\n   - `ranges_to_expr`: 1 range → `Str` if `start == end` else `Range`; otherwise `CharClass`.\n   - `coalesce_run`: emits only if `merged.len() < run.len()`.\n   - All-qualify → coalesce whole chain or leave unchanged; some-qualify → contiguous runs of ≥3 qualifying alternatives coalesced individually, others untouched, order preserved.\n   - `coalesce_seq`: `Seq(NegPred(inner), Ident("ANY"))` where every alternative of `inner` qualifies (single alternative included) → `NegCharClass(merged)`; otherwise the `Seq` is rebuilt unchanged. Terminates on finite trees; no recursion on cycles.\n\n3. `generator/src/generator.rs` — arms in **both** `generate_expr` and `generate_expr_atomic`:\n   `state.match_char_by(|c| matches!(c, #(#start..=#end)|*))` built with `quote!` over the ranges (char literals from each `String`\'s first char), and `!matches!(...)` for `NegCharClass`.\n\n4. `vm/src/lib.rs` `parse_expr` — `CharClass`/`NegCharClass` arms using `state.match_char_by(|c| ranges.iter().any(|(s, e)| ...))` with inclusive char comparisons (negated for `NegCharClass`).\n\n**Expected test fallout (as you predicted):** `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs::tests::rotate` (`Choice(Str a, Str b, Str c, Str d)` → `CharClass([("a","d")])`) and any other exact-output assertions over single-char choices will fail; `skip`-style tests are unaffected because the skipper pass already converts those to `Skip` before the coalescer runs. I could not verify this by running the suite.\n\nTo proceed, the session needs either an operator approval path for subagent tool use, `SANDBOX_POLICY=off` set deliberately, or the task re-run at depth 0 where write tools are permitted.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1046, 'prompt_tokens': 47125, 'tota