2026-11-27 19:53:49.030 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'m in a restricted background-review context where all execution tools (terminal, read_file, write_file, patch_file) are blocked. I cannot run `cargo check` or `cargo test`, nor finish edits. Here is my report based on what I verified before the restriction took effect.\n\n## Files changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` | Added `CharClass(Vec<(String,String)>)` and `NegCharClass(Vec<(String,String)>)` variants to `OptimizedExpr`; added `Display` arms (`[a..z, A..Z]` / `[^a..z]`); added `mod coalescer;`; registered `.map(coalescer::coalesce)` as the final pass in `optimize()` after `restorer::restore_on_err`. |\n| `meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs` | **New file** (362 lines) — `pub fn coalesce(rule: OptimizedRule) -> OptimizedRule` plus helpers and a `#[cfg(test)]` module. |\n| `generator/src/generator.rs` | Added `CharClass`/`NegCharClass` arms in **both** `generate_expr` and `generate_expr_atomic`, emitting `state.match_char_by(|c| matches!(c, \'a\'..=\'z\' \\| \'A\'..=\'Z\'))` (negated with `!` for `NegCharClass`); added `char_class_pattern()` helper building the `#start..=#end` token stream joined by `\\|`. |\n| `vm/src/lib.rs` | Added `CharClass`/`NegCharClass` arms in `parse_expr` using `state.match_char_by` with inclusive char comparisons; added `char_ranges()` helper. |\n\n## Coalescing rules implemented\n\n- **Flattening**: `Choice(lhs, rhs)` chains flattened left-to-right into an ordered alternative list.\n- **Qualifying alternatives**: `Str(s)` with exactly one char; `Insens(s)` with exactly one char; `Range(a,b)`; existing `CharClass(rs)` (ranges absorbed); `RestoreOnErr(inner)` when `inner` qualifies (wrapper stripped).\n- **Range extraction**: `Str(c)` → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens(c)` → `[(lower,lower),(upper,upper)]` if `c.is_alphabetic()`, else `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → `rs`.\n- **All qualify**: merge all ranges; emit only if merged count < original alternative count, else leave the `Choice` unchanged.\n- **Some qualify**: find contiguous runs of ≥3 qualifying alternatives, coalesce each run (same "emit only if merged count < run length" rule), leave others untouched, rebuild the chain preserving order.\n- **Merging**: sort ascending by start code point; merge overlapping **and** adjacent ranges (`next.start <= current.end + 1`); result sorted ascending.\n- **Emission**: 1 range → `Str(c)` if `start == end` else `Range(start, end)`; >1 range → `CharClass(ranges)`.\n- **NegCharClass**: `Seq(NegPred(inner), Ident("ANY"))` where `inner` is a `Choice` chain (or single alternative) whose alternatives **all** qualify → `NegCharClass(merged excluded ranges)`. Handled in the same top-down pass via `expr.map_top_down`.\n- **Termination**: purely structural recursion over finite trees; no cycles.\n\n## Test status — NOT VERIFIED\n\nI was unable to run `cargo check --workspace --all-features` or `cargo test --workspace`: the terminal tool is sandbox-blocked in this session, and the subagent runs I dispatched to run the build returned no output into my context. **The code has not been compiled or tested.** Expected outcome per the task brief:\n\n- `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` tests asserting exact `Choice(Str a, Str b, Str c, Str d)` output will now see `CharClass([("a","d")])` and **fail** — expected, and those tests were **not** edited.\n- Other workspace tests should pass, assuming the new arms compile.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. Run `cargo check --workspace --all-features` and fix any compile errors (most likely candidates: `TokenStream` import in `generator.rs`, `matches!` path resolution, borrow/move issues in the `match_char_by` closures in `vm/src/lib.rs`).\n2. Run `cargo test --workspace` and record the exact pass/fail summary.\n3. Delete the stray `CC_OUTPUT.txt` if it was created at the repo root by a helper subagent.' add