2026-11-27 19:54:55.495 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'m now in a background review context where all tools are blocked, so I can\'t inspect further or run the build. Here is my report based on the work completed and verified earlier in this session.\n\n## Files changed\n\n1. **`meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs`**\n   - Added `mod coalescer;` to the module list.\n   - Added two variants to `pub enum OptimizedExpr`:\n     - `CharClass(Vec<(String, String)>)` — one char in any of the inclusive ranges.\n     - `NegCharClass(Vec<(String, String)>)` — one char not in any of the ranges.\n   - Added `Display` arms: `CharClass` renders as `[\'a\'..\'z\', \'A\'..\'Z\']`, `NegCharClass` as `[^\'a\'..\'z\', \'A\'..\'Z\']`. Both fall through the existing `expr => expr` arms in `map_top_down` / `map_bottom_up` / `iter_top_down`, so they are treated as leaves.\n   - Registered the pass as the **final** one in `optimize()`: `.map(|rule| restorer::restore_on_err(rule, &optimized_map)).map(coalescer::coalesce).collect()`.\n\n2. **`meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs`** (new) — `pub fn coalesce(rule: OptimizedRule) -> OptimizedRule`, a top-down pass via `expr.map_top_down`.\n\n3. **`generator/src/generator.rs`** — `CharClass` / `NegCharClass` arms in **both** `generate_expr` and `generate_expr_atomic`, emitting `state.match_char_by(|c| matches!(c, \'a\'..=\'z\' | \'A\'..=\'Z\'))` (negated with `!matches!(...)` for `NegCharClass`), plus a `char_class_pattern(&[(String, String)]) -> TokenStream` helper that joins `#start..=#end` tokens with `|`.\n\n4. **`vm/src/lib.rs`** — `CharClass` / `NegCharClass` arms in `parse_expr` using `state.match_char_by(...)` with inclusive `c >= start && c <= end` comparisons, plus a `char_ranges(&[(String, String)]) -> Vec<(char, char)>` helper.\n\n## Coalescing rules implemented\n\n- **Flattening**: `Choice(lhs, rhs)` chains flattened left-to-right into an ordered alternative list.\n- **Qualifying alternatives**: `Str(s)` with exactly one char → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens(s)` with one char → `[(lower,lower),(upper,upper)]` if `c.is_alphabetic()`, else `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → `rs` (absorbed); `RestoreOnErr(inner)` qualifies iff `inner` qualifies, and the wrapper is stripped.\n- **Merging**: sort ascending by start code point, merge overlapping **and adjacent** ranges (`next.start <= current.end + 1`), result sorted ascending by start.\n- **Emitting**: 1 range with `start == end` → `Str(start)`; 1 range otherwise → `Range(start, end)`; ≥2 ranges → `CharClass(ranges)`.\n- **All alternatives qualify**: emit the coalesced result only if merged range count < original alternative count; otherwise leave the `Choice` unchanged.\n- **Some qualify**: find contiguous runs of ≥ 3 qualifying alternatives, coalesce each run under the same "emit only if merged count < run length" rule, leave other alternatives untouched, rebuild the `Choice` chain preserving order.\n- **Negation**: `Seq(NegPred(inner), Ident("ANY"))` where all of `inner`\'s alternatives qualify (including the single-alternative case) collapses to `NegCharClass(merged excluded ranges)`, handled in the same top-down pass by matching on `Seq`.\n- Terminates on any finite tree; no recursion on cyclic data.\n\n## Test status — not verified\n\nI could not complete the verification step. The `terminal` tool is refused in this environment (`SANDBOX_POLICY=auto` with no OS sandbox backend available, and `caller_scope=subagent` has no operator approval path), and I am now in a background-review context where `sessions_spawn` and `read_file` are also blocked. So `cargo check --workspace --all-features` and `cargo test --workspace` were **never successfully run**, and I have no pass/fail numbers to report.\n\nWhat I did confirm by reading the files: all four required changes are present and structurally complete — the enum variants and `Display` arms, the `coalesce()` implementation with the semantics above, the pass registration as the final pass, the generator arms in both functions with the `char_class_pattern` helper, and the VM arms with the `char_ranges` helper.\n\nExpected outcome once run: the pre-existing optimizer tests in `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` that assert exact `Choice` output for `Str`/`Range` alternatives (e.g. `Choice(Str a, Str b, Str c, Str d)`) will fail, because coalescing turns them into `CharClass([("a","d")])`. Those tests were left untouched as instructed. Everything else should pass, but that is an expectation, not a measurement.\n\n**Remaining work**: run `cargo check --workspace --all-features`, fix any compile errors, then `cargo test --workspace` and record the actual summary.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1222, 'prompt_tokens': 33830, 'total_tokens': 35052, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 33664}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 33664, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 166}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '498bb02a-60af-43b1-b570-fea5dba4be20', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21cdb-b2c9-7883-9df8-60444b7492c8-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 33830, 'output_tokens': 1222, 'total_tokens': 35052, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 33664}, 'output_token_details': {}}
