sce(rule: OptimizedRule) -> OptimizedRule` — one top-down pass via `expr.map_top_down(...)`.\n   - Helpers: `flatten_choice`, `build_choice`, `qualifying_ranges`, `merge_ranges`, `emit_ranges`, `coalesce_run`, `coalesce_choice`, `coalesce_seq`, `negated_ranges`.\n\n3. **`generator/src/generator.rs`**\n   - `CharClass` / `NegCharClass` arms in **both** `generate_expr` and `generate_expr_atomic`, emitting `state.match_char_by(|c| matches!(c, #pattern))` and `state.match_char_by(|c| !matches!(c, #pattern))`.\n   - New `char_class_pattern(&[(String, String)]) -> TokenStream` helper.\n\n4. **`vm/src/lib.rs`**\n   - `CharClass` / `NegCharClass` arms in `parse_expr` using `state.match_char_by(move |c| ranges.iter().any(|&(start, end)| c >= start && c <= end))`, negated for `NegCharClass`.\n   - New `char_ranges(&[(String, String)]) -> Vec<(char, char)>` helper.\n\n## Coalescing rules implemented\n\n- **Flatten**: `Choice(lhs, rhs)` chains flattened left-to-right into an ordered alternative list; rebuilt right-nested by `build_choice`.\n- **Qualification**: `Str(s)` with exactly one char → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens(s)` with exactly one char → `[(lower,lower),(upper,upper)]` if `c.is_alphabetic()`, else `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → `rs` (absorbed); `RestoreOnErr(inner)` qualifies iff `inner` qualifies, wrapper stripped in output.\n- **Merging**: sort ascending by start code point; merge when `next.start <= current.end + 1` (overlapping **and** adjacent); result sorted ascending by start.\n- **Emission**: exactly 1 range with `start == end` → `Str(start)`; exactly 1 range otherwise → `Range(start, end)`; ≥2 ranges → `CharClass(ranges)`.\n- **All alternatives qualify**: merge all; emit only if `merged.len() < alternatives.len()`, else leave the `Choice` unchanged.\n- **Some qualify**: contiguous runs of ≥3 qualifying alternatives are coalesced with the same `merged.len() < run.len()` guard; other alternatives untouched; `Choice` chain rebuilt preserving order.\n- **NegCharClass**: `Seq(NegPred(inner), Ident("ANY"))` → `NegCharClass(merged)` when all of `inner`\'s alternatives qualify (a single qualifying alternative goes through the same flatten path). `Skip` nodes from the skipper pass are left alone.\n- **Termination**: recursion only via `map_top_down` over a finite tree; no cyclic traversal.\n\n## Test status\n\n**Unknown — not executed.** Expected outcome per the task brief: the pre-existing optimizer tests in `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` that assert exact `Choice` output for `Str`/`Range` alternatives (e.g. `rotate`, and any test expecting `Choice(Str a, Str b, Str c, Str d)`) will fail, because coalescing now yields `CharClass([("a","d")])`. Those tests were **not** edited, as instructed.\n\n## Outstanding items\n\n1. **Stray artifacts not deleted** — `CC_OUTPUT.txt`, `CHECK_OUTPUT.txt`, `TEST_OUTPUT.txt` in the repo root (written by blocked child subagents) are still present; deletion requires execution, which is blocked. Remove them before committing.\n2. **Compile verification** — needs a shell with execution permission. Most likely failure points to check first: `matches!` resolution in generated code (prelude is fine; use `::core::matches!` if a `no_std` build complains), and any unused-import warnings in `coalescer.rs`.\n3. **Test run** — confirm the only failures are the pre-existing exact-`Choice` optimizer assertions.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1409, 'prompt_tokens': 37611, 'total_tokens': 39020, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 37376}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 37376, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 235}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': 'a82f7f61-77de-4e8b-af8c-1fc3d8bbf1ef', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21cdc-b153-77c0-9574-72f0f4e9d33d-0' tool_calls=[] 