e_seq`, `negated_ranges`.\n\n**`generator/src/generator.rs`** — `CharClass`/`NegCharClass` arms added to both `generate_expr` and `generate_expr_atomic`, plus a `char_class_pattern` helper.\n\n**`vm/src/lib.rs`** — `CharClass`/`NegCharClass` arms in `parse_expr`, plus a `char_ranges` helper.\n\n## What I could NOT complete\n\n- The rigorous manual compile review you asked for (re-reading the variant placement against every exhaustive match, the `map_top_down` closure signature, `emit_ranges` return types, the `>= 3` run rule, the `merged.len() < original count` guard, empty-range panic paths, `OptimizedExpr` imports, trailing-`|` in the token stream, closure borrows in the VM). I got as far as confirming the pass registration and locating the four `RestoreOnErr` match sites in `restorer.rs`; then `read_file`, `search_files`, and `ast_grep_search` were all blocked mid-review.\n- Deleting the stray `CC_OUTPUT.txt`, `CHECK_OUTPUT.txt`, `TEST_OUTPUT.txt` from the repo root — that needs a shell, which is refused.\n\n## Files changed (implementation)\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` | `mod coalescer;`; `CharClass(Vec<(String,String)>)` + `NegCharClass(Vec<(String,String)>)` variants; `Display` impls (`[a..z, A..Z]`, `[^a..z]`); `.map(coalescer::coalesce)` as final pass |\n| `meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs` | **new** — `pub fn coalesce` top-down pass |\n| `generator/src/generator.rs` | arms in `generate_expr` + `generate_expr_atomic`; `char_class_pattern` helper |\n| `vm/src/lib.rs` | arms in `parse_expr`; `char_ranges` helper |\n\n## Rules implemented\n\n- **Flatten**: `Choice(lhs, rhs)` chains flattened left-to-right; rebuilt right-nested.\n- **Qualify**: `Str(s)` one char → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens(s)` one char → alphabetic gives `[(lower,lower),(upper,upper)]`, else `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → `rs` absorbed; `RestoreOnErr(inner)` qualifies iff inner does, wrapper stripped.\n- **Merge**: sort ascending by start code po