(OptimizedExpr) -> OptimizedExpr`, which satisfies `FnMut`. The closure is passed by value and the function is `Copy`, so no move issue.\n\n**2. Borrow/move patterns — OK**\n- `flatten_choice(expr: OptimizedExpr, out: &mut Vec<OptimizedExpr>)` takes ownership and pushes `*lhs` / descends `*rhs` — both are `Box<OptimizedExpr>` derefs producing owned values, so no partial-move conflict (each `Box` is consumed exactly once).\n- `build_choice(mut alts: Vec<OptimizedExpr>) -> OptimizedExpr` pops from the end (`alts.pop().expect(...)`) and folds right-to-left, so the resulting chain is correctly right-nested and order-preserving. The `.expect` is unreachable because `flatten_choice` always pushes ≥1 element.\n- `merge_ranges(mut ranges: Vec<(char, char)>) -> Vec<(char, char)>` sorts in place then folds into a new `Vec` — no aliasing.\n- `emit_ranges(ranges: Vec<(char, char)>) -> OptimizedExpr` matches on `ranges.len()` and moves the single element out via `into_iter().next()`; the `>= 2` branch maps to `(String, String)` pairs. No borrow escapes.\n\n**3. Exhaustive-match fallout from the two new variants — OK**\nVerified by AST search that the only matches over `OptimizedExpr` outside the ones I extended are in `restorer.rs` (4 sites, all with catch-all arms) and `mod.rs`\'s `map_top_down`/`map_bottom_up`/`iter_top_down`/`Display`, which all end in `expr => expr` / `_ =>` catch-alls. `generator.rs` and `vm/src/lib.rs` both have catch-all `_ => unreachable!()`-style tails, and I added explicit arms before them. No non-exhaustive match remains.\n\n**4. `quote!` token construction — OK**\n`char_class_pattern` iterates with `enumerate()` and emits `|` **only when `index > 0`**, then `#start..=#end`. No trailing `|`. An empty slice yields an empty `TokenStream` (unreachable in practice: `CharClass` is only emitted with ≥2 ranges). `TokenStream::extend` accepts a `TokenStream`, which is what `quote!` returns.\n\n**5. Char extraction in generator and vm — OK**\nBoth use `start.chars().next().expect("empty char literal")` on the `String`, yielding a `char`. In the generator the `char` is interpolated into `quote!` as a char literal (`\'a\'`), which `quote` supports natively. In the VM, `char_ranges` maps `(String, String)` → `(char, char)` into an owned `Vec`, and the closure is `move`, so it takes ownership of that `Vec` — no borrow of `expr` escapes the match arm.\n\n**Suspected compile errors found by review: none.**\n\n**Residual risk (cannot be checked without a compiler):** clippy/rustfmt lints (one long line in `coalescer.rs`), and `matches!` resolution in generated code if a `no_std` build complains — switch to `::core::matches!` if so.\n\n### Files changed\n1. `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` — `mod coalescer;`, `.map(coalescer::coalesce)` as final pass, two new variants, two `Display` arms.\n2. `meta/src/optimizer/coalescer.rs` — **new**, 362 lines.\n3. `generator/src/generator.rs` — arms in `generate_expr` + `generate_expr_atomic`, `char_class_pattern` helper.\n4. `vm/src/lib.rs` — arms in `parse_expr`, `char_ranges` helper.\n\nStray `CC_OUTPUT.txt`, `CHECK_OUTPUT.txt`, `TEST_OUTPUT.txt` deleted.\n\n### Coalescing rules implemented\n- **Flatten** `Choice(lhs, rhs)` chains left-to-right; rebuild right-nested.\n- **Qualify**: `Str` (1 char) → `[(c,c)]`; `Insens` (1 char) → alphabetic ? `[(lower,lower),(upper,upper)]` : `[(c,c)]`; `Range(a,b)` → `[(a,b)]`; `CharClass(rs)` → `rs`; `RestoreOnErr(inner)` iff inner qualifies (wrapper stripped).\n- **Merge**: sort ascending by start; merge when `next.start <= current.end + 1` (overlapping **and** adjacent).\n- **Emit**: 1 range with `start == end` → `Str`; 1 range otherwise → `Range`; ≥2 → `CharClass`.\n- **All qualify**: emit only if `merged.len() < alternatives.len()`, else leave `Choice` untouched.\n- **Some qualify**: coalesce contiguous runs of ≥3 with the same guard; leave others untouched; rebuild preserving order.\n- **NegCharClass**: `Seq(NegPred(inner), Ident("ANY"))` → `NegCharClass(merged)` when all inner alternatives qualify. `Skip` nodes left alone.\n- **Termination**: only `map_top_down` recursion over a finite tree.\n\n### Test status\n**Not run — blocked.** Expected once run: the pre-existing optimizer tests in `meta/src/optimizer/mod.rs` asserting exact `Choice` output for `Str`/`Range` alternatives (e.g. `rotate`) will fail, since coalescing now yields `CharClass([("a","d")])`. Those tests were **not** edited, as instructed.\n\n**Next steps**: run the two commands above from a privileged shell; fix any lint/compile fallout; run `cargo fmt` before committing.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2774, 'prompt_tokens': 44381, 'total_tokens': 47155, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 44160}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 44160, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 221}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '2db7ba2f-db24-4584-9cb7-744b80888e9b', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21cdd-e1a7-7d91-83ed-e223c64fa9aa-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 44381, 'output_tokens': 2774, 'total_tokens': 47155, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 44160}, 'output_token_details': {}}
